  {
   "id": "soviet-union-outline",
   "note": "Cliopatria draws Czechoslovakia inside the Soviet Union in 1969-1990, the years Soviet troops were stationed there after the 1968 invasion, and parts of Afghanistan as Soviet territory in 1979-1989. Czechoslovakia remained a separate state, and Afghanistan was ruled by its own communist government. The Soviet Union's frontiers did not change between 1953 and Lithuania's declaration of independence in 1990, so its 1953-1968 outline is used for 1969-1989 and its 1991 outline for 1990.",
