   "id": "afghanistan-1979-1991",
   "note": "With the Soviet outline trimmed to the Soviet Union itself (soviet-union-outline), Afghanistan is drawn whole in 1979-1991, with the border data's own outline of 1976-1978, which fits the Soviet outline. Afghanistan's borders did not change. (That outline, like the border data's for every year from 1919, puts a strip north of the Amu Darya around Termez on the Afghan side.) The Democratic Republic of Afghanistan (from 1987 the Republic of Afghanistan) held Kabul and the main cities until April 1992; the war maps show the areas each side controlled.",
